---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { codeThemes } from '../../code-themes';
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import Example from '../../components/Example.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Theming"
  description="Theme Elo UI with design tokens: light and dark mode, density, the warm theme, and your own brand."
>
  <h1>Theming</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every color, radius, and spacing value is a CSS custom property. Load the base theme, optionally
    a theme on top, and override semantic tokens to match your brand.
  </p>

  <h2>Light and dark</h2>
  <p>
    The theme follows the user's color scheme. Set <code>data-elo-theme="light"</code> or
    <code>"dark"</code> on any element to force a theme for that part of the page.
  </p>
  <Example
    code={`<div data-elo-theme="dark" style="padding: 1rem; background: var(--elo-color-bg); border-radius: 8px">
  <elo-button variant="primary">Always dark</elo-button>
</div>`}
  />

  <h2>Density</h2>
  <p>
    Set <code>data-elo-density="compact"</code> on any element for tighter controls in data-heavy
    screens. Try it with the Density menu at the top of this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Warm theme</h2>
  <p>
    A second look ships with the package: stone grays, a teal accent, rounder corners, and softer
    shadows, in light and dark. Import it after the base theme. Preview it with the Style menu at
    the top of this page.
  </p>
  <Code
    code={`import '@elo-ui/core/theme.css';
import '@elo-ui/core/themes/warm.css';`}
    lang="js"
    themes={codeThemes}
  />

  <h2>Your own brand</h2>
  <p>
    Override semantic tokens, not primitives, and define both light and dark values with the same
    selectors the base theme uses.
  </p>
  <Code
    code={`:root,
[data-elo-theme='light'] {
  --elo-color-accent: #7c3aed;
  --elo-color-accent-hover: #6d28d9;
  --elo-color-accent-active: #5b21b6;
  --elo-color-accent-text: #6d28d9;
  --elo-color-focus-ring: #7c3aed;
}

[data-elo-theme='dark'] {
  --elo-color-accent-text: #c4b5fd;
  --elo-color-focus-ring: #a78bfa;
}

@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root:not([data-elo-theme='light']) {
    --elo-color-accent-text: #c4b5fd;
    --elo-color-focus-ring: #a78bfa;
  }
}`}
    lang="css"
    themes={codeThemes}
  />

  <h2>Keeping it accessible</h2>
  <p>
    Every theme Elo UI ships is checked automatically against WCAG AA in light and dark: text on
    every background (4.5:1), button text on accent and danger colors, all five status variants, and
    control borders and focus rings (3:1). When you set your own colors, check these pairs:
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Foreground</th>
          <th>Background</th>
          <th>Minimum</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>--elo-color-accent-fg</code>
          </td>
          <td>
            <code>--elo-color-accent</code>, <code>-hover</code>
          </td>
          <td>4.5:1</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>--elo-color-accent-text</code>
          </td>
          <td>
            <code>--elo-color-surface</code>
          </td>
          <td>4.5:1</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>--elo-color-fg-muted</code>
          </td>
          <td>
            <code>--elo-color-surface</code>, <code>--elo-color-bg</code>
          </td>
          <td>4.5:1</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>--elo-color-border-control</code>
          </td>
          <td>
            <code>--elo-color-surface</code>
          </td>
          <td>3:1</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>--elo-color-focus-ring</code>
          </td>
          <td>
            <code>--elo-color-surface</code>, <code>--elo-color-bg</code>
          </td>
          <td>3:1</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</Docs>
